in bloodstream forms of <italic>Trypanosoma brucei</italic> is energized by the electrogenic pumping of protons catalysed by the F<sub>1</sub>F<sub>0</sub>-ATPase.</article-title><source>Eur J Biochem</source><volume>209</volume><fpage>207</fpage><lpage>216</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">1327770</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="ppat.1000436-Opperdoes1"><label>7</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Opperdoes</surname><given-names>FR</given-names></name><name><surname>Borst</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name><name><surname>De Rijke</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name></person-group><year>1976</year><article-title>Oligomycin Sensitivity of the Mitochondrial Atpase as a Marker for Fly Transmissability and the Presence of Functional Kinetoplast DNA in African Trypanosomes.</article-title><source>Comp Biochem Physiol (B)</source><volume>55B</volume><fpage>25</fpage><lpage>30</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">133016</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="ppat.1000436-Walker1"><label>8</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Walker</surname><given-names>JE</given-names></name><name><surname>Dickson</surname><given-names>VK</given-names></name></person-group><year>2006</year><article-title>The peripheral stalk of the mitochondrial ATP synthase.</article-title><source>Biochim Biophys Acta</source><volume>1757</volume><fpage>286</fpage><lpage>296</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16697972</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="ppat.1000436-von1"><label>9</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>von</surname><given-names>BC</given-names></name><name><surname>Cook</surname><given-names>GM</given-names></name><name><surname>Dimroth</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name></person-group><year>2008</year><article-title>Unique rotary ATP synthase and its biological diversity.</article-title><source